The diagram shows the curve $y = g(x)$. Over which values of $x$ is the curve concave up?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
             xmin=-5.0, xmax=3.3, ymin=-6.4, ymax=8.1, samples=100, clip=false,
             xtick={-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3}, ytick={-6,-4,-2,2,4,6}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-4.19:2.2] {0.3*(x*x*x + 3*x*x)};
\node[font=\small] at (axis cs:1.7,1.9) {$y=g(x)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
